1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,640
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,640 --> 00:00:04,990
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:04,990 --> 00:00:06,150
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:09,130
I've been a lineman for
thirty-two years.

5
00:00:09,240 --> 00:00:12,000
Climbing poles in spikes
and a harness,

6
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:13,795
kneeling in a bucket
truck,

7
00:00:13,795 --> 00:00:15,200
storm calls in the middle

8
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:16,030
of the night,

9
00:00:16,030 --> 00:00:18,570
jumping down off the truck
more times

10
00:00:18,570 --> 00:00:19,750
than I could ever count.

11
00:00:19,790 --> 00:00:20,930
That's a lot of years

12
00:00:20,930 --> 00:00:22,240
on a pair of knees.

13
00:00:22,460 --> 00:00:23,450
I had my right knee

14
00:00:23,450 --> 00:00:24,990
replaced two years ago.

15
00:00:25,080 --> 00:00:26,840
It has hurt every day
since.

16
00:00:27,270 --> 00:00:28,690
Not surgery pain.

17
00:00:28,730 --> 00:00:30,160
I know what that felt
like,

18
00:00:30,160 --> 00:00:31,140
and it went away.

19
00:00:31,533 --> 00:00:32,540
This is different.

20
00:00:32,580 --> 00:00:33,200
Tight.

21
00:00:33,240 --> 00:00:33,830
Full.

22
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:34,880
Like a band around

23
00:00:34,880 --> 00:00:36,550
the joint that never
loosens.

24
00:00:36,700 --> 00:00:37,750
And for two years I've

25
00:00:37,750 --> 00:00:39,030
been told the same thing.

26
00:00:39,260 --> 00:00:40,310
Give it time.

27
00:00:40,480 --> 00:00:42,450
At six weeks it was
swelling,

28
00:00:42,450 --> 00:00:43,850
and swelling is normal.

29
00:00:43,980 --> 00:00:44,830
At three months,

30
00:00:44,830 --> 00:00:45,880
give it six.

31
00:00:46,010 --> 00:00:46,740
At six months,

32
00:00:46,740 --> 00:00:48,250
some knees take a full
year.

33
00:00:48,290 --> 00:00:49,260
At a year,

34
00:00:49,260 --> 00:00:51,240
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

35
00:00:51,420 --> 00:00:52,350
And I didn't just wait.

36
00:00:52,390 --> 00:00:53,790
We went down the list.

37
00:00:53,900 --> 00:00:55,350
More physical therapy.

38
00:00:55,430 --> 00:00:56,520
Every session,

39
00:00:56,520 --> 00:00:58,020
every exercise at home.

40
00:00:58,390 --> 00:00:59,490
I got stronger.

41
00:00:59,810 --> 00:01:01,380
The tightness never moved.

42
00:01:01,440 --> 00:01:02,780
The pain pills helped,

43
00:01:02,780 --> 00:01:04,040
and that was the problem.

44
00:01:04,210 --> 00:01:06,060
I'm already on enough
every morning,

45
00:01:06,060 --> 00:01:07,370
and nobody could tell me

46
00:01:07,370 --> 00:01:08,520
when I'd get to stop.

47
00:01:08,560 --> 00:01:09,865
Then a nerve block.

48
00:01:09,905 --> 00:01:11,610
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

49
00:01:11,650 --> 00:01:12,960
And after that, a second

50
00:01:12,960 --> 00:01:14,000
operation to go back

51
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:14,980
in and do it over.

52
00:01:15,360 --> 00:01:16,320
I said no.

53
00:01:16,560 --> 00:01:18,860
Every morning I laced up
my boots

54
00:01:18,860 --> 00:01:19,930
and my knee felt like

55
00:01:19,930 --> 00:01:21,540
a band was wrapped around
it,

56
00:01:21,540 --> 00:01:24,290
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

57
00:01:24,700 --> 00:01:26,400
Every morning I took
something

58
00:01:26,400 --> 00:01:27,980
for it and went to work.

59
00:01:28,330 --> 00:01:29,970
I couldn't climb anymore,

60
00:01:29,970 --> 00:01:31,470
so they kept me in the
bucket.

61
00:01:31,810 --> 00:01:33,490
Couldn't kneel in that
bucket long

62
00:01:33,490 --> 00:01:34,660
enough to finish a job

63
00:01:34,660 --> 00:01:36,640
without shifting off the
knee,

64
00:01:36,640 --> 00:01:38,420
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's game

65
00:01:38,420 --> 00:01:40,480
without shifting every two
minutes.

66
00:01:40,720 --> 00:01:41,990
It woke me at night,

67
00:01:41,990 --> 00:01:43,840
and it turned ordinary
things,

68
00:01:43,840 --> 00:01:45,510
like climbing up into the
truck

69
00:01:45,510 --> 00:01:47,080
or getting up off the
couch,

70
00:01:47,080 --> 00:01:48,150
into a decision.

71
00:01:48,270 --> 00:01:49,560
After a long and serious

72
00:01:49,560 --> 00:01:50,680
talk with my wife,

73
00:01:50,680 --> 00:01:52,350
I went back in one more
time.

74
00:01:52,729 --> 00:01:53,920
That was the fourth set

75
00:01:53,920 --> 00:01:55,460
of X-rays on this knee.

76
00:01:55,750 --> 00:01:57,080
And like the three before
it,

77
00:01:57,080 --> 00:01:59,700
the answer was everything
looks great.

78
00:01:59,810 --> 00:02:02,050
No loosening, no
infection,

79
00:02:02,050 --> 00:02:03,120
nothing wrong.

80
00:02:03,230 --> 00:02:04,350
Only this time

81
00:02:04,350 --> 00:02:05,790
there was no new number.

82
00:02:06,020 --> 00:02:08,310
Nobody said give it
another six months.

83
00:02:08,490 --> 00:02:10,420
There was nothing left to
give it.

84
00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:11,870
I sat in the parking

85
00:02:11,870 --> 00:02:12,930
lot for a while.

86
00:02:13,240 --> 00:02:14,650
Okay, I thought.

87
00:02:14,941 --> 00:02:16,280
Then explain this.

88
00:02:16,430 --> 00:02:18,550
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

89
00:02:18,550 --> 00:02:20,150
I hit my breaking point.

90
00:02:20,280 --> 00:02:22,280
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

91
00:02:22,610 --> 00:02:23,500
I'd just come in off

92
00:02:23,500 --> 00:02:24,670
a storm call,

93
00:02:24,670 --> 00:02:26,230
twelve hours of putting
lines

94
00:02:26,230 --> 00:02:27,360
back up in the rain.

95
00:02:27,720 --> 00:02:29,680
Everyone in the house was
asleep

96
00:02:29,680 --> 00:02:31,500
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

97
00:02:31,500 --> 00:02:32,640
with my leg up,

98
00:02:32,640 --> 00:02:34,340
trying to find any angle
where

99
00:02:34,340 --> 00:02:35,960
it didn't feel like
something was wrapped

100
00:02:35,960 --> 00:02:37,730
around my knee and
tightening.

101
00:02:37,910 --> 00:02:40,110
My wife didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

102
00:02:40,320 --> 00:02:41,980
By then I'd stopped
telling her.

103
00:02:42,600 --> 00:02:43,750
And I just thought,

104
00:02:43,750 --> 00:02:45,640
is this really my life
now?

105
00:02:45,870 --> 00:02:47,660
Thirty-two years on the
line,

106
00:02:47,660 --> 00:02:48,810
and I was starting to
wonder

107
00:02:48,810 --> 00:02:49,700
if this knee was going

108
00:02:49,700 --> 00:02:50,480
to make me hang up

109
00:02:50,480 --> 00:02:52,300
my belt before I was
ready.

110
00:02:52,440 --> 00:02:53,950
I can't live like this.

111
00:02:54,183 --> 00:02:56,040
So I made myself a
promise.

112
00:02:56,150 --> 00:02:56,950
I wouldn't go a day

113
00:02:56,950 --> 00:02:58,510
without looking for an
answer.

114
00:02:58,720 --> 00:03:00,040
And when I found one,

115
00:03:00,040 --> 00:03:01,290
I'd share it with everyone

116
00:03:01,290 --> 00:03:02,730
going through the same
thing.

117
00:03:02,970 --> 00:03:04,380
So I got my laptop

118
00:03:04,380 --> 00:03:05,450
out and went looking.

119
00:03:05,490 --> 00:03:06,590
Not for a product.

120
00:03:06,630 --> 00:03:07,770
For an explanation.

121
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:09,750
Mayo Clinic forums,

122
00:03:09,750 --> 00:03:12,220
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

123
00:03:12,220 --> 00:03:13,620
doctor videos,

124
00:03:13,620 --> 00:03:15,200
medical animations.

125
00:03:15,430 --> 00:03:16,910
And that's when I found a
video

126
00:03:16,910 --> 00:03:18,640
from a physical therapist
named Dr.

127
00:03:18,680 --> 00:03:20,070
Steven Salinger,

128
00:03:20,070 --> 00:03:21,390
whose own wife had been

129
00:03:21,390 --> 00:03:23,090
through exactly this.

130
00:03:23,358 --> 00:03:25,480
But before I say anything
else,

131
00:03:25,480 --> 00:03:26,920
I want to be straight with
you.

132
00:03:27,330 --> 00:03:29,430
You've already had
something work fast.

133
00:03:29,470 --> 00:03:30,300
The ice.

134
00:03:30,572 --> 00:03:32,360
The first week of a new
pill.

135
00:03:32,628 --> 00:03:34,140
The good day after a
session.

136
00:03:34,180 --> 00:03:35,550
Then it wore off.

137
00:03:35,910 --> 00:03:38,130
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

138
00:03:38,525 --> 00:03:40,200
Fast relief isn't relief.

139
00:03:40,650 --> 00:03:41,680
It's a preview.

140
00:03:41,857 --> 00:03:42,860
So I'm not going to tell

141
00:03:42,860 --> 00:03:44,170
you this works fast.

142
00:03:44,210 --> 00:03:45,140
It doesn't.

143
00:03:45,400 --> 00:03:47,230
But if you're willing to
be patient,

144
00:03:47,230 --> 00:03:48,350
and to look at what's
going

145
00:03:48,350 --> 00:03:49,980
on around your new knee

146
00:03:49,980 --> 00:03:51,370
instead of inside it,

147
00:03:51,370 --> 00:03:52,840
there is a real reason

148
00:03:52,840 --> 00:03:54,030
it still hurts.

149
00:03:54,220 --> 00:03:56,010
And something you can do
about it.

150
00:03:56,540 --> 00:03:58,240
Let me explain what he
said,

151
00:03:58,240 --> 00:03:59,380
because this is what
changed

152
00:03:59,380 --> 00:04:00,500
everything for me.

153
00:04:00,700 --> 00:04:02,400
He started with the
basics.

154
00:04:02,440 --> 00:04:04,000
A knee replacement takes
out

155
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:05,610
the worn joint surfaces

156
00:04:05,610 --> 00:04:07,620
and puts in metal and
plastic.

157
00:04:07,890 --> 00:04:09,770
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

158
00:04:09,770 --> 00:04:11,500
you had before the
operation.

159
00:04:11,740 --> 00:04:13,210
That part I already knew.

160
00:04:13,783 --> 00:04:14,990
But then he explained
something

161
00:04:14,990 --> 00:04:16,350
nobody had ever told me.

162
00:04:16,520 --> 00:04:16,970
He said,

163
00:04:16,970 --> 00:04:18,530
think about a swollen foot

164
00:04:18,530 --> 00:04:19,860
inside a shoe.

165
00:04:20,040 --> 00:04:21,500
The shoe didn't shrink.

166
00:04:21,760 --> 00:04:23,865
Your foot is taking up
more room,

167
00:04:23,865 --> 00:04:25,580
so everything feels
cramped

168
00:04:25,580 --> 00:04:27,300
and tight and squeezed.

169
00:04:27,700 --> 00:04:28,840
Your new knee sits

170
00:04:28,840 --> 00:04:30,300
in a limited space with
living

171
00:04:30,300 --> 00:04:32,010
tissue packed all around
it.

172
00:04:32,510 --> 00:04:34,080
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

173
00:04:34,080 --> 00:04:35,690
had to work through that
tissue.

174
00:04:35,970 --> 00:04:38,560
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

175
00:04:38,920 --> 00:04:40,250
At first that's normal.

176
00:04:40,400 --> 00:04:42,050
But in some people that
swelling can

177
00:04:42,050 --> 00:04:44,680
stay switched on far
longer than expected.

178
00:04:44,980 --> 00:04:46,600
And swollen tissue takes
up more

179
00:04:46,600 --> 00:04:48,300
room than calm tissue
does.

180
00:04:48,520 --> 00:04:50,050
So when you bend,

181
00:04:50,050 --> 00:04:51,750
that tissue gets
compressed.

182
00:04:51,790 --> 00:04:53,040
When you straighten,

183
00:04:53,040 --> 00:04:54,320
it gets pulled tight.

184
00:04:54,480 --> 00:04:55,720
That's the band.

185
00:04:55,843 --> 00:04:58,320
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

186
00:04:58,390 --> 00:04:59,420
And you start being

187
00:04:59,420 --> 00:05:00,600
the one who says,

188
00:05:00,600 --> 00:05:01,690
you guys go ahead.

189
00:05:01,730 --> 00:05:02,770
I'll stay here.

190
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:04,760
And that's exactly why so
much

191
00:05:04,760 --> 00:05:06,550
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

192
00:05:06,945 --> 00:05:08,940
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

193
00:05:08,940 --> 00:05:09,820
around the knee.

194
00:05:10,100 --> 00:05:10,870
Worth doing,

195
00:05:10,870 --> 00:05:11,810
and I'd done it.

196
00:05:12,040 --> 00:05:13,550
It does nothing about
tissue

197
00:05:13,550 --> 00:05:14,630
taking up room.

198
00:05:14,920 --> 00:05:16,170
A nerve block quiets

199
00:05:16,170 --> 00:05:17,800
the nerve carrying the
signal.

200
00:05:17,960 --> 00:05:20,000
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

201
00:05:20,160 --> 00:05:21,730
But when that irritated
tissue

202
00:05:21,730 --> 00:05:23,510
finally calms down,

203
00:05:23,510 --> 00:05:25,103
it holds less fluid,

204
00:05:25,103 --> 00:05:26,710
and it takes up less room.

205
00:05:26,970 --> 00:05:28,340
Less room taken up means

206
00:05:28,340 --> 00:05:30,290
less pressure squeezing
the joint.

207
00:05:30,440 --> 00:05:32,120
That's what takes the
pressure off.

208
00:05:32,410 --> 00:05:33,650
After two years of this,

209
00:05:33,650 --> 00:05:35,170
it finally made sense.

210
00:05:35,255 --> 00:05:36,930
The problem was never the
new knee.

211
00:05:36,970 --> 00:05:38,832
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

212
00:05:38,872 --> 00:05:40,270
He calls it the squeeze.

213
00:05:40,407 --> 00:05:42,330
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

214
00:05:42,600 --> 00:05:43,780
I'd bought knee sleeves,

215
00:05:43,780 --> 00:05:45,330
compression braces,

216
00:05:45,330 --> 00:05:47,260
gel knee pads for the
bucket,

217
00:05:47,260 --> 00:05:49,940
creams, half of Amazon
really,

218
00:05:49,940 --> 00:05:51,520
and all any of it gave

219
00:05:51,520 --> 00:05:52,660
me was an hour.

220
00:05:52,730 --> 00:05:53,770
I even looked at going

221
00:05:53,770 --> 00:05:55,610
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

222
00:05:55,650 --> 00:05:57,180
But at $200 a session

223
00:05:57,180 --> 00:05:59,229
with nothing covered by
insurance,

224
00:05:59,229 --> 00:06:00,580
that was a quick no.

225
00:06:00,869 --> 00:06:01,890
Then one night I went

226
00:06:01,890 --> 00:06:03,160
back to that knee
replacement

227
00:06:03,160 --> 00:06:04,500
group and actually read
it.

228
00:06:04,875 --> 00:06:06,070
Thousands of people,

229
00:06:06,070 --> 00:06:07,480
years out from surgery,

230
00:06:07,480 --> 00:06:08,740
comparing notes on
stiffness

231
00:06:08,740 --> 00:06:10,430
and tightness nobody could
explain.

232
00:06:10,678 --> 00:06:12,090
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

233
00:06:12,090 --> 00:06:13,820
the same thing kept coming
up.

234
00:06:14,120 --> 00:06:15,170
This one device,

235
00:06:15,170 --> 00:06:16,730
and people saying it was
the first

236
00:06:16,730 --> 00:06:18,580
thing that made a
difference.

237
00:06:18,690 --> 00:06:21,458
And before anyone jumps in
thinking, alright,

238
00:06:21,458 --> 00:06:22,270
here it comes,

239
00:06:22,270 --> 00:06:23,780
he's selling me something,

240
00:06:23,780 --> 00:06:25,530
let me shut that down
right now.

241
00:06:25,810 --> 00:06:27,370
I'm only here because I
made myself

242
00:06:27,370 --> 00:06:29,380
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

243
00:06:29,380 --> 00:06:30,220
that if I ever found

244
00:06:30,220 --> 00:06:31,030
something that helped,

245
00:06:31,030 --> 00:06:31,940
I'd say so.

246
00:06:32,470 --> 00:06:33,850
It's called the KenRelief
Red

247
00:06:33,850 --> 00:06:34,970
Light Therapy Wrap.

248
00:06:35,010 --> 00:06:36,220
At first glance

249
00:06:36,220 --> 00:06:37,200
I didn't buy it.

250
00:06:37,420 --> 00:06:39,300
It looked like the cheap
knee sleeves

251
00:06:39,300 --> 00:06:41,800
off Amazon that did
nothing for me.

252
00:06:41,986 --> 00:06:44,160
But I went to their
website anyway,

253
00:06:44,160 --> 00:06:45,100
just to see what all

254
00:06:45,100 --> 00:06:46,230
the fuss was about.

255
00:06:46,440 --> 00:06:48,290
It's the same red light
therapy clinics

256
00:06:48,290 --> 00:06:52,290
charge $200 a session for,
off machines

257
00:06:52,290 --> 00:06:54,220
that cost fifty thousand
dollars,

258
00:06:54,220 --> 00:06:55,170
in a wrap you plug

259
00:06:55,170 --> 00:06:56,320
into the wall at home.

260
00:06:56,360 --> 00:06:58,160
Two hundred and forty
lights.

261
00:06:58,320 --> 00:07:00,710
Red at 660 nanometers

262
00:07:00,710 --> 00:07:03,420
and near-infrared at 850,

263
00:07:03,420 --> 00:07:06,190
run together for the
strongest effect.

264
00:07:06,486 --> 00:07:07,860
Four strength levels.

265
00:07:08,230 --> 00:07:10,140
A five to thirty minute
timer.

266
00:07:10,242 --> 00:07:11,790
Then I saw the guarantee.

267
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:13,270
Ninety days.

268
00:07:13,440 --> 00:07:15,750
Results or your money
back,

269
00:07:15,750 --> 00:07:17,040
no questions,

270
00:07:17,040 --> 00:07:18,330
no store credit,

271
00:07:18,330 --> 00:07:20,010
and you don't even send it
back.

272
00:07:20,050 --> 00:07:22,500
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

273
00:07:22,500 --> 00:07:24,250
days to change my mind.

274
00:07:24,380 --> 00:07:25,730
There wasn't much to lose,

275
00:07:25,730 --> 00:07:26,760
so I ordered it.

276
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:28,240
Two of them, actually.

277
00:07:28,520 --> 00:07:30,624
Only the right knee was
replaced,

278
00:07:30,624 --> 00:07:32,584
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

279
00:07:32,584 --> 00:07:34,330
and I'd done it for two
years.

280
00:07:34,370 --> 00:07:35,440
Every time I jumped down

281
00:07:35,440 --> 00:07:36,450
off that truck,

282
00:07:36,450 --> 00:07:37,890
I landed on the left.

283
00:07:38,120 --> 00:07:40,240
The left one was carrying
the difference.

284
00:07:40,430 --> 00:07:41,540
When it came,

285
00:07:41,540 --> 00:07:44,170
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

286
00:07:44,170 --> 00:07:45,450
because I'd been let down
too

287
00:07:45,450 --> 00:07:47,020
many times to get excited.

288
00:07:47,360 --> 00:07:48,770
What I felt was warmth.

289
00:07:48,810 --> 00:07:50,570
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

290
00:07:50,680 --> 00:07:52,270
More like it was coming
from inside

291
00:07:52,270 --> 00:07:54,270
the knee and spreading
around it.

292
00:07:54,620 --> 00:07:55,500
And that was it.

293
00:07:55,850 --> 00:07:57,500
That was the whole
experience.

294
00:07:57,730 --> 00:07:59,090
When I took it off,

295
00:07:59,090 --> 00:08:00,310
I'll be honest,

296
00:08:00,310 --> 00:08:02,060
nothing dramatic had
happened.

297
00:08:02,300 --> 00:08:03,760
And after what that video
said,

298
00:08:03,760 --> 00:08:06,030
that's exactly what I
expected.

299
00:08:06,250 --> 00:08:07,580
What was different

300
00:08:07,580 --> 00:08:08,600
was that for the first

301
00:08:08,600 --> 00:08:10,150
time in two years

302
00:08:10,150 --> 00:08:12,040
I'd done something for my
knee

303
00:08:12,040 --> 00:08:13,100
instead of to it.

304
00:08:13,510 --> 00:08:14,570
Twenty minutes,

305
00:08:14,570 --> 00:08:15,740
in my own chair.

306
00:08:15,780 --> 00:08:17,270
No drive, no copay.

307
00:08:17,310 --> 00:08:18,680
They say twenty minutes.

308
00:08:18,760 --> 00:08:19,610
I did thirty,

309
00:08:19,610 --> 00:08:20,540
twice a day,

310
00:08:20,540 --> 00:08:22,530
lowest setting that first
week.

311
00:08:22,640 --> 00:08:23,710
Once before work,

312
00:08:23,710 --> 00:08:24,830
once when I got home.

313
00:08:25,100 --> 00:08:26,390
I put it on the calendar.

314
00:08:26,630 --> 00:08:27,530
The first week,

315
00:08:27,530 --> 00:08:28,420
I couldn't have told

316
00:08:28,420 --> 00:08:30,040
you if anything was
happening.

317
00:08:30,140 --> 00:08:31,030
I tried not to get

318
00:08:31,030 --> 00:08:31,940
my hopes up.

319
00:08:32,220 --> 00:08:33,130
I'd had things help

320
00:08:33,130 --> 00:08:34,760
for a week and then stop.

321
00:08:34,979 --> 00:08:36,500
But somewhere in the
second week I

322
00:08:36,500 --> 00:08:38,570
noticed I'd come down the
stairs

323
00:08:38,570 --> 00:08:40,080
without holding the rail.

324
00:08:40,250 --> 00:08:41,630
I hadn't decided to.

325
00:08:41,820 --> 00:08:43,050
I just did it,

326
00:08:43,050 --> 00:08:44,690
then stopped halfway down

327
00:08:44,690 --> 00:08:46,040
because I realized.

328
00:08:46,200 --> 00:08:47,780
By the end of the fourth
week

329
00:08:47,780 --> 00:08:48,840
I'd slept through the
night

330
00:08:48,840 --> 00:08:50,070
four times running.

331
00:08:50,340 --> 00:08:51,410
I stood at the counter

332
00:08:51,410 --> 00:08:52,907
and finished making dinner

333
00:08:52,907 --> 00:08:54,500
without looking for the
stool.

334
00:08:54,600 --> 00:08:56,110
None of that is dramatic.

335
00:08:56,150 --> 00:08:57,060
All of it was gone

336
00:08:57,060 --> 00:08:58,140
for two years.

337
00:08:58,300 --> 00:08:59,830
A few weeks later my wife
asked

338
00:08:59,830 --> 00:09:00,660
if I wanted to walk

339
00:09:00,660 --> 00:09:02,250
the long way around the
block.

340
00:09:02,647 --> 00:09:03,500
And for the first time

341
00:09:03,500 --> 00:09:04,070
in two years,

342
00:09:04,070 --> 00:09:05,080
I said yes.

343
00:09:05,120 --> 00:09:06,870
I wanted to understand
why,

344
00:09:06,870 --> 00:09:08,360
so I read the whole thing.

345
00:09:08,410 --> 00:09:10,090
It comes down to four
steps.

346
00:09:10,130 --> 00:09:10,820
One.

347
00:09:11,070 --> 00:09:13,260
The tissue around a new
knee

348
00:09:13,260 --> 00:09:14,700
can stay inflamed

349
00:09:14,700 --> 00:09:16,600
long after surgery is
over.

350
00:09:17,010 --> 00:09:17,630
Two.

351
00:09:17,780 --> 00:09:20,670
Inflamed tissue holds
extra fluid,

352
00:09:20,670 --> 00:09:21,640
so it takes up more

353
00:09:21,640 --> 00:09:22,920
room than it should.

354
00:09:23,375 --> 00:09:23,730
Three.

355
00:09:23,770 --> 00:09:25,830
There's only so much room
in there.

356
00:09:25,920 --> 00:09:27,420
Bending compresses it.

357
00:09:27,495 --> 00:09:29,430
Straightening pulls it
tight.

358
00:09:29,520 --> 00:09:30,790
That's the squeeze.

359
00:09:30,880 --> 00:09:31,590
Four.

360
00:09:31,950 --> 00:09:33,850
Red and near-infrared
light have been

361
00:09:33,850 --> 00:09:36,180
studied for calming that
inflammation,

362
00:09:36,180 --> 00:09:37,570
so the swelling and the
pressure

363
00:09:37,570 --> 00:09:38,840
can come down with it.

364
00:09:39,150 --> 00:09:40,300
In a randomized trial,

365
00:09:40,300 --> 00:09:42,170
patients given light
therapy after

366
00:09:42,170 --> 00:09:44,670
a knee replacement had
less pain,

367
00:09:44,670 --> 00:09:46,690
less swelling and better
early

368
00:09:46,690 --> 00:09:48,380
movement than those who
weren't.

369
00:09:48,670 --> 00:09:51,480
A 2025 review said the
same,

370
00:09:51,480 --> 00:09:52,960
and was clear the evidence

371
00:09:52,960 --> 00:09:54,050
is still limited.

372
00:09:54,310 --> 00:09:56,510
I probably sound like a
broken record

373
00:09:56,510 --> 00:09:57,990
to the guys on my crew.

374
00:09:58,512 --> 00:10:00,570
But after two years of
doing everything

375
00:10:00,570 --> 00:10:02,710
I was told and getting
nowhere,

376
00:10:02,710 --> 00:10:04,610
you have no idea what it's

377
00:10:04,610 --> 00:10:06,480
like to sleep through the
night,

378
00:10:06,480 --> 00:10:08,363
say yes to the walk,

379
00:10:08,363 --> 00:10:09,770
and get my life back.

380
00:10:10,030 --> 00:10:11,610
So take it from me.

381
00:10:11,910 --> 00:10:13,470
Don't spend another year
waiting

382
00:10:13,470 --> 00:10:14,540
for it to settle.

383
00:10:14,580 --> 00:10:16,500
Don't spend two hundred a
session.

384
00:10:16,660 --> 00:10:18,190
More than ten thousand
people

385
00:10:18,190 --> 00:10:19,190
with pain after a knee

386
00:10:19,190 --> 00:10:21,712
replacement have already
tried this.

387
00:10:21,752 --> 00:10:23,280
Some had it worse than I
did.

388
00:10:23,660 --> 00:10:24,810
You can get the KenRelief

389
00:10:24,810 --> 00:10:26,420
wrap from their website,

390
00:10:26,420 --> 00:10:27,750
with a discount link

391
00:10:27,750 --> 00:10:29,390
and ninety days to try it.

392
00:10:29,800 --> 00:10:31,810
If it doesn't do anything
for you,

393
00:10:31,810 --> 00:10:33,120
you get your money back

394
00:10:33,120 --> 00:10:34,370
